#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7d017c2-e3ff-56d9-9334-9ac4fa843657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-19x+30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304686} {:answer/id #uuid "3c61eea0-6b09-573a-b969-b636455c3741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-38x-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304687} {:answer/id #uuid "151c154c-d125-5381-9ace-152bee787a80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+47x+60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304688} {:answer/id #uuid "e58c95f7-87e5-56a0-956d-88829d4e8f33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+19x+60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304689} {:answer/id #uuid "1ceb7ee0-935f-5b83-9144-6119f5574980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ceb7ee0-935f-5b83-9144-6119f5574980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304690} :answer-field/id #uuid "753ec0e2-b325-5183-8e84-914a8d2e5340" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5046e0c1-2f8b-58f5-a21d-913e91899338" :question/math-academy-id "q-104467" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-1.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-1(x-(-5))(x-(-4))(x-(-3)) \\\\  & =-(x+5)(x+4)(x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(x+5)(x+4)(x+3) & =-({x}^{2}+9x+20)(x+3) \\\\  & =-({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}+27x+20x+60) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60.$"}]}
